# Which tracked paths are public. Each line is `public <path>` or `private <path>`, and
# every tracked path falls under exactly one line. A new top-level path needs a line.
# This repository is published whole, so `private` doesn't mean unpublished: a push sends
# every tracked file, the two marked `private` below included. Here it means published
# but not read by the residue scan, the check run before a push that looks for private
# names and reference ids in published files. `.residue-allow` lists text that scan and
# the tag check let stand as data, so it would trip the scan by design.
public .gitattributes
public .github
public .gitignore
public .nvmrc
public LICENSE
public README.md
public package-lock.json
public package.json
public packages
public pyproject.toml
public tools
public uv.lock
private .public-paths
private .residue-allow
